#: ../../kitchen-sink/typography.rst:4
msgid ""
"The opening paragraph of a page introduces it, so it is drawn a little "
"larger. Everything after it is body text at a comfortable measure, with "
"**strong text**, *emphasis*, ``inline code``, :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+P`, "
":guilabel:`Save as`, :menuselection:`File --> Export --> PDF`, a `link to"
" daisyUI <https://daisyui.com>`_, a reference to :doc:`admonitions`, a "
"cross-reference to :py:func:`textwrap.dedent`, an abbreviation "
":abbr:`WCAG (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines)`, subscript H\\ "
":sub:`2`\\ O and superscript E = mc\\ :sup:`2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../kitchen-sink/typography.rst:11
msgid ""
"A second paragraph shows how body text reads at length. Documentation is "
"read in short bursts by people who arrived from a search or a link, so "
"the first sentence of each paragraph should carry its point, and the rest"
" should support it. Line length, line height and the space between "
"paragraphs matter more than the typeface."
msgstr ""

